{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Terror and dread fall upon them.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): אימתה — upon the near; and פחד — upon the far, in the manner of what is written (Joshua 2:10): ״כי שמענו את אשר הוביש ה׳ את מי ים סוף מפניכם״. And the word אימתה is like אימה, with the extra תי״ו, and likewise (Psalms 44:27): ״קומה עזרתה לנו״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: אימתה is the fear of HaShem that receives from פחד. And thus Moses prayed that the attribute of judgment be drawn out against their enemies. And this last ה׳ in the Name — it is the Shekhinah that was with the Ark, and this is what is said (I Samuel 4:17): ״וארון האלהים נלקחה״, for he should have said נלקח, but this indicates the attachment of the Shekhinah to the Ark. And therefore we find that the Ark is called by the name YHWH, as it is written (Numbers 10:36): ״ובנחה יאמר שובה ה׳״ and ״ובנוח ה׳״ — that is, when the Ark journeyed and when the Ark rested, they would say ״קומה ה׳ שובה ה׳״, and he did not say קום שוב. And furthermore, the word ובנחה with a ה׳ indicates the feminine when it is final in the word — it was said, it was called; also the Shekhinah is called in the feminine, for the Targum of (Exodus 33:14) ״פני ילכו״ is ״שכינתי תהך״ and he did not translate יהך. And the Kabbalah is thus — that it is תהך in the feminine. And behold, the Shekhinah, which is the seal of the structure, receives power from the attribute of גבורה called פחד. Therefore it says ״תפול עליהם אימתה ופחד״ — that is, the fear of the Shekhinah, which receives emanation from פחד. And this is clear." "<b>Until Your people pass, YHWH.</b> This is the crossing of the wadis of Arnon. ״Until Your people pass״ — this is the crossing of the Jordan, in the manner of what is written (Joshua 3:15–17): ״וכבא נושאי הארון עד הירדן ורגלי הכהנים נושאי הארון נטבלו בקצה המים״ etc., and ״ויעמדו הכהנים נושאי הארון ברית ה׳ בחרבה בתוך הירדן״. Thus Onkelos, of blessed memory, translated." "<b>This people You acquired.</b> Above he mentioned ״This people You redeemed״, because he speaks of the splitting of the Sea of Reeds, before the Torah was given. And here, when he mentions the crossing of the wadis of Arnon and the crossing of the Jordan — and they had already received the Torah — he said, ״This people You acquired״, because they had become the acquisition of the Holy One, blessed be He, through the Torah He had already given them." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> ״This people You acquired״ — four things are called an acquisition: Israel, as is said, ״This people You acquired״; the Torah, as is said (Proverbs 8:22): ״HaShem acquired me, the first of His way״; heaven and earth, as is said (Genesis 14:19): ״Acquirer of heaven and earth״; the Temple, as is said (Psalms 78:54): ״This mountain Your right hand acquired״. Let Israel, who are called an acquisition, come and receive the Torah, which is called an acquisition; by whose merit stand heaven and earth, which are called an acquisition; and let them build the Temple, which is called an acquisition."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :register {:fixes 1}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:59:46.438358895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}